title: "Arabidopsis Spaceflight Omics: Biomarker Discovery and Single-Cell Atlas Integration"
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Richard
    family-names: Barker
    affiliation: "GeneLab Plant Analysis Working Group, NASA Open Science Data Repository"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8368-2825"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dr-richard-barker/arabidopsis-spaceflight-omics"
abstract: >
  A multi-track computational pipeline for identifying spaceflight-responsive
  biomarker genes in Arabidopsis thaliana using NASA OSDR transcriptomic data,
  validating them against a single-cell seedling atlas with scPlantLLM, and
  characterizing cell-cell communication patterns with PlantCellChat. The LASSO
  biomarker panel (85 genes, AUC=0.734) reveals stress/ER-proteostasis enrichment
  in flight-upregulated genes and flavonoid metabolism in ground-upregulated genes.
  Ca2+ signaling dominates cell-cell communication (strength=249.5, 10.2x over K+).
  A CBL9-CIPK23-AKT1 crosstalk circuit connects Ca2+ sensing to K+ uptake, with
  guard cells as the primary signaling hub. Includes Sankey diagram, ggPlantmap
  spatial montage, and full supplementary methods.
keywords:
  - Arabidopsis thaliana
  - spaceflight
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - LASSO regression
  - cell-cell communication
  - PlantCellChat
  - scPlantLLM
  - ggPlantmap
  - GO enrichment
  - NASA OSDR
